  "rules": {
    "summary": "2026-27: 18 clubs play a double round robin (34 rounds, 14 August 2026 to 23 May 2027); 16th, 17th and 18th go down to the TFF 1. Lig. Teams level on points are ranked by the games between them: points, then goal difference (away goals do not count), then goals for three or more teams, then overall goal difference and goals scored. The TFF's own table applies head-to-head only once the teams level have played each other home and away (its 2026-27 table after six rounds ranks every tie by goal difference; its 2025-26 final table ranks Kocaelispor above Alanyaspor and Gaziantep, and Kayserispor above Fatih Karagümrük, by head-to-head).",
    "sources": [
      "https://www.tff.org/Resources/TFF/Documents/STATULER/2026-2027/2026-2027-sezonu-super-lig-musabakalari-statusu.pdf",
      "https://www.tff.org/Resources/TFF/Documents/TALIMATLAR/Futbol-Musabaka-Talimati.pdf",
      "https://www.tff.org/default.aspx?pageID=198",
      "https://www.tff.org/default.aspx?pageID=1768"
    ]
  },
  "notes": [
    "Backtested on the Süper Lig's 2023-24 to 2025-26 seasons (1,024 matches): week-ahead predictions score 0.197 (ranked probability score) against 0.226 for home/draw/away base rates."
